.SS Percent
.B %
computes y*x/100,
.B %t
computes 100*x/y and
.B %chg
computes 100*(x\-y)/y. All three leave Y in place, as on the HP.
.SS Registers
.B n regidx
selects register
.I n
(0\-99). Then
.BR sto ", " sto+ ", " sto\- ", " sto* ", " sto/
and
.B rcl
act on it.
.B sto
leaves X on the stack.
.SS Statistics
.B s+
takes x from X and y from Y and pushes the count;
.B s\-
removes a pair exactly. Standard deviations are sample values (n\-1).
.B lr
leaves the slope in Y and the intercept in X;
.BR yhat " and " xhat
evaluate the regression line.
.SS Angles
.BR deg ", " rad " and " grad
set the angle mode. In degrees and grads, multiples of a quarter turn
give exact results.
.BR >p " and " >r
convert between rectangular and polar coordinates;
.BR >hms " and " >h
between decimal hours and H.MMSS.
.SS Display
.BR fix ", " sci ", " eng " (exponent a multiple of 3) and " all
(15 significant digits) select the format;
.B n p
sets the number of digits (0\-15). FIX falls back to SCI when a value
does not fit.
.SH NUMERICAL METHODS
A function is a word (or built-in) that maps X to f(X), leaving exactly
one value.
.B \(aq name
pushes its execution token; the numerical words consume that token:
.nf
a b \(aq f integrate     integral over [a,b] (tanh-sinh, bisecting where needed)
a b \(aq f romberg       the same by Romberg extrapolation
a b \(aq f fzero         root in a bracket with a sign change (Brent)
g   \(aq f solve         root near one guess (bracket search, then Brent)
a b \(aq f minimize      argument of the minimum in [a,b] (Brent)
x   \(aq f deriv         f\(aq(x) (Ridders\(aq extrapolation)
lo hi \(aq f fsum        sum of f(i) for integers lo..hi
lo hi \(aq f fprod       product of f(i)
\(aq f exec             run f
.fi
.PP
.B x tol
sets the tolerance (default 1e-10, relative to max(1,|result|)).
.B nevals
gives the number of function evaluations of the last call,
.B interr
the error estimate of the last integral, and
.B internals
shows the current settings. Functions run on the live stack and may use
registers and other words; an error inside one aborts the call and the
stack rolls back; Ctrl-C interrupts.
.PP
An integrable singularity at an endpoint converges to full precision when
that endpoint is 0; elsewhere the result is good to about 1e-8 and a
warning is printed. Shift the variable if that matters.
.PP
.nf
: f dup * 2 \- ;    0 3 \(aq f fzero      \e" sqrt 2
: g 1 + inv ;       0 1 \(aq g integrate  \e" ln 2
0 pi \(aq sin integrate                  \e" 2
.fi
.SH USER WORDS
.nf
: name body ;      \e" may span several lines
( comment )        \e" needs spaces around the parentheses
\e comment          \e" to end of line
.fi
.PP
A word is compiled when it is defined, so an unknown name in the body is
reported immediately. Calls are resolved by name at run time, so
redefining a word also changes its callers. A word may call itself;
recursion stops at 256 levels and Ctrl-C interrupts a running word.
.PP
Control flow works inside definitions and at top level, where the rest of
the line is compiled and run as one unit. The 1.x spellings
.BR DO ", " LOOP ", " IF ", " ELSE ", " THEN " and " I
are accepted:
.nf
flag if ... [else ...] then
begin ... flag until
begin ... flag while ... repeat
limit start do ... i ... loop      \e" skipped when start = limit
limit start do ... n +loop         \e" n < 0 counts down to limit
.fi
.B i
is the innermost loop index and
.B j
the next outer one.
.PP
.nf
: fac  dup 1 > if dup 1 \- fac * then ;
: sum  ( n \-\- 1+..+n ) 0 swap 1 + 1 do i + loop ;
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mm_14/words.txt
Saved words, one per line: name followed by body. Loaded at startup
unless
.B \-n
is given. A 1.x
.I user_words.txt
is read when this file does not exist.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mm_14/registers.txt
Saved registers: index and value per line.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mm_14/history
Readline history, last 1000 lines.
.PP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
defaults to
.IR ~/.config .
Saves write a temporary file and rename it, so an interrupted save does
not damage the previous file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. In batch mode, 1 if any error was reported, 2 for a usage
error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ mm_14 \-e "2 10 ^"
1024.000000
$ echo "all 1 3 /" | mm_14
0.333333333333333
$ mm_14 \-n \-e ": f dup * 2 - ; 0 3 ' f fzero"
1.414214
$ mm_14 \-f script.rpn
.fi
